  "notes": "Adds explicit Correct/Incorrect feedback for a real pending automatic blowing decision in Settings -> AI. Feedback is tied to the decision and AI-enable epoch, consumed once by the backend owner and reported as queued, saved or not saved. Silence and USB QA do not become training labels. Ratings do not directly change outputs.\n\nRefreshes automatic blowing and BLE preference displays without resetting selection focus. Keeps the existing flashlight learning records and adaptive-profile storage layout. The base TFLM network remains hand-weighted; the separate logistic adapter learns from explicit attributed feedback. No model-accuracy claim is made.\n\nVerification: selected production-source host checks and the ESP32-S3 build. Runtime installation and captured UI evidence are recorded separately in the QA report. The conditional rating panel requires a genuine pending decision; a default-page capture does not prove hardware rating or learning. Full load/power lifecycle, physical LED appearance and physical-phone OTA acceptance remain separate open QA items.\n",
